From 46e9cf38fe0a3f5a8451d4824f32479ee5203b0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nuubOS <nuubos@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:54:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Cheaper TA parsing and drawing (nuubOS)

On the libretro thread, which reads and draws each frame:

- Translucent strips are merged like opaque ones, each into the one
  before when they share every setting (~85 % of them in Dead or Alive 2,
  Test Drive Le Mans and Shenmue II): every draw call costs several
  microseconds in Panfrost on a Cortex-A53. The order is kept; with
  per-strip auto-sort a merged strip is sorted as one.
- make_index() no longer reads every vertex back to leave out the
  invalid ones: they are noted as they are made (inf_vertices), and only
  a polygon with one is checked. Reading ~1.5 MB of vertices back, gone
  from the cache by then, was most of its time (11.5 -> 3 % of the
  thread). It also writes the indices through a local pointer.
- Vertex colours are put together and stored as one word: stored a byte
  at a time (chars, which may alias anything) they made the compiler
  reload the face colour and the vertex list after each byte.
- The vertex and index buffers are filled through an unsynchronised
  mapping (the fence of the ring says they are idle), not
  glBufferSubData.

Upstream: not submitted (nuubOS H700 tuning).
